{"name":"Casket","hex":"#a49186","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"casket","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A little box, e.g. for jewellery.","An urn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put into, or preserve in, a casket."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/casket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffin","blocks":[{"text":"A coffin or casket is a funerary box used for viewing or keeping a corpse, for burial, entombment or cremation. Coffins are sometimes referred to as caskets, particularly in American English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/CoffinShopWarsaw.jpg/330px-CoffinShopWarsaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffin","wikidata":"Q184418"},{"title":"Casket (decorative box)","blocks":[{"text":"A casket is a decorative box or container that is usually smaller than a chest and is typically decorated. In recent centuries they are often used as boxes for jewelry, but in earlier periods they were also used for keeping important documents and many other purposes. Many ancient caskets are reliquaries, for both Buddhist and Christian relics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Jewelry_casket_MET_DP241007_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Jewelry_casket_MET_DP241007_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casket_(decorative_box)","wikidata":"Q639460"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/A_casket_showroom_in_Billings%2C_Montana.jpg/500px-A_casket_showroom_in_Billings%2C_Montana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/A_casket_showroom_in_Billings%2C_Montana.jpg/1280px-A_casket_showroom_in_Billings%2C_Montana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th